  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only config (config_005: scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) achieves 0.650 acc, while the only multimodal test (config_030: same RNA/image/aggregation but concat fusion) achieves 0.632 acc — slightly worse. This single data point suggests the image modality (resnet50) may be adding noise rather than signal, but the difference is small (~1.8%) and could reflect the fusion method rather than the modality itself. Question: config_031 isolates the fusion method (weighted vs. concat) while holding all other design choices identical to config_030. If weighted fusion recovers or exceeds config_005's performance, the image modality has latent value and is worth further investment (e.g., better image encoders). If it does not, we gain strong evidence to redirect the remaining budget toward RNA-only optimization. Why this is best: it is the most controlled, single-variable comparison available that directly resolves the strategic question of whether to pursue multimodal or focus on RNA-only, making the most efficient use of a limited experiment slot."
}

